
# Build outputs
# Disassembly output that contains verbatim ROM bytes
# Editor / OS noise
# Emulator save files (battery SRAM / states) — runtime artifacts, ROM-adjacent
# Emulator snapshots / state (MAME writes snap/<driver>/)
# Extracted / converted game data (build artifacts derived from the ROM)
# Local Claude Code settings (machine-specific)
# MAME emulator artifacts (it writes config/nvram into CWD subdirs)
# Rule 5: never commit copyrighted / ROM-derived material.
# The user's source ROM (any GB ROM in the tree)
# Working copy of the symbol file that mgbdis auto-loads (generated from symbols/sml.sym,
# which IS tracked — it holds our hand-authored RE labels, not ROM bytes).
*.1bpp
*.2bpp
*.chr
*.gb
*.gbc
*.lst
*.lvl
*.map
*.o
*.pal
*.s0
*.sav
*.srm
*.ss0
*.sv
.DS_Store
.claude/
/cfg/*.cfg.bak
/cfg/default.cfg
/cfg/svision.cfg
/super-mario-land-gb.sym
build/
disasm/
extracted/
snap/
*.ss[0-9]
*.sgm
level select and invincible.cheats

# Rule 5 (belt-and-suspenders): cheat codes, save RAM, savestates are ROM-adjacent
*.cheats
*.ram
*.gb.ram
*.ss[0-9]
*.ss
